1
00:00:20,199 --> 00:00:21,719
As a high school dropout,

2
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:25,000
my job options are pretty limited.

3
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:29,039
And most of them aren't easy.

4
00:00:30,879 --> 00:00:32,840
But compared to what I went through,

5
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:36,479
this life is more than enough for me.

6
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,880
I only have one problem.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:44,000
I don't dare stay at any job for too long.

8
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:48,159
Because I'm terrified of dealing with people.

9
00:00:49,159 --> 00:00:52,280
I just want to live in peace.

10
00:01:29,159 --> 00:01:31,079
You've had quite a few jobs.

11
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,480
Even though it's just a waiter job,

12
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:37,920
our standards here

13
00:01:38,079 --> 00:01:40,359
are much stricter than elsewhere.

14
00:01:40,719 --> 00:01:42,719
Are you sure you can handle it?

15
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,480
Do you just not like to talk,

16
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:52,280
or can't you speak?

17
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:58,840
I don't like to talk.

18
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,159
Good habit.

19
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,840
Let's do a one-month trial then.

20
00:03:05,719 --> 00:03:06,680
It's fine, it's fine, it's fine.

21
00:03:07,039 --> 00:03:07,960
Just keep eating.

22
00:03:08,319 --> 00:03:09,240
It's covered in dirt.

23
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:12,879
Um...

24
00:03:15,039 --> 00:03:15,800
Thanks.

25
00:03:17,599 --> 00:03:18,360
For what?

26
00:03:22,199 --> 00:03:23,120
The plating.

27
00:03:25,439 --> 00:03:28,439
It's fine. I made mistakes at first too.

28
00:03:31,159 --> 00:03:31,919
Go ahead and eat.

29
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:49,599
Sir, do you have a reservation?

30
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,319
My last name is Zhou. Number ending in 0070.

31
00:03:54,159 --> 00:03:55,319
Right this way, Mr. Zhou.

32
00:04:04,479 --> 00:04:05,120
Mr. Zhou.

33
00:04:05,439 --> 00:04:07,599
Your table is ready. This way.

34
00:04:16,319 --> 00:04:16,879
Qianqian.

35
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:17,920
Come sit down.

36
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:21,959
Mr. Zhou, I'll take care of everything then.

37
00:04:21,959 --> 00:04:23,000
Alright, go ahead.

38
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,839
Excuse me, could we get two glasses of water?

39
00:04:28,839 --> 00:04:29,480
Sure, right away.

40
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:30,480
Thank you.

41
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:48,000
That was when I finally understood

42
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,040
that everything you run away from

43
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,680
won't let you go so easily.

44
00:04:56,519 --> 00:04:57,199
What's wrong?

45
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,439
Nothing.

46
00:05:05,079 --> 00:05:06,959
Then you take Xiao Yu this week.

47
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:09,399
Sure. Sunday, right?

48
00:05:09,439 --> 00:05:11,319
I have a meeting this weekend,

49
00:05:11,319 --> 00:05:12,399
and then two surgeries.

50
00:05:12,519 --> 00:05:13,079
Thanks.

51
00:05:13,279 --> 00:05:14,839
I should be done around four.

52
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,959
Okay, I'll go. What are you doing then?

53
00:05:17,199 --> 00:05:17,920
Me...

54
00:05:19,759 --> 00:05:21,079
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

55
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:26,319
So sorry.

56
00:05:26,319 --> 00:05:27,120
Sorry, I'm so sorry.

57
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,199
It didn't spill on you two, did it?

58
00:05:28,279 --> 00:05:28,879
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

59
00:05:28,879 --> 00:05:29,959
I'll clean it up right away.

60
00:05:29,959 --> 00:05:30,600
Be careful.

61
00:05:30,639 --> 00:05:31,759
Yes, yes. I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

62
00:05:32,079 --> 00:05:32,839
Are you okay?

63
00:05:34,199 --> 00:05:35,120
Sorry to bother you two.

64
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:50,480
I told you, the rules here are strict.

65
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,600
I won't ask you why,

66
00:05:55,839 --> 00:05:56,720
and I don't care.

67
00:05:57,279 --> 00:05:58,439
If it happens again,

68
00:05:59,959 --> 00:06:00,839
you're out.

69
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:27,199
Want a midnight snack?

70
00:06:40,439 --> 00:06:41,199
Stolen?

71
00:06:42,199 --> 00:06:43,399
How could I?

72
00:06:45,079 --> 00:06:47,800
I made it from leftover ingredients.

73
00:06:58,839 --> 00:06:59,519
How is it?

74
00:07:01,959 --> 00:07:02,720
I'm okay.

75
00:07:09,279 --> 00:07:10,639
Why did you help me?

76
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:12,439
Aren't people supposed to

77
00:07:13,079 --> 00:07:14,560
help each other out?

78
00:07:15,199 --> 00:07:16,000
Are they?

79
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,680
The people I used to know

80
00:07:20,839 --> 00:07:21,959
were nothing like that.

81
00:07:25,199 --> 00:07:26,199
That's normal.

82
00:07:27,759 --> 00:07:28,839
Everyone only helps

83
00:07:28,879 --> 00:07:30,319
their own kind, right?

84
00:07:35,319 --> 00:07:36,639
Are we the same kind?

85
00:07:38,439 --> 00:07:39,319
I don't know.

86
00:07:41,439 --> 00:07:42,639
I don't really know you yet.

87
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:44,879
But I just get the feeling

88
00:07:46,759 --> 00:07:48,120
you could leave at any moment.

89
00:07:57,959 --> 00:07:58,759
What about you?

90
00:08:00,319 --> 00:08:01,680
Haven't you thought of leaving?

91
00:08:04,439 --> 00:08:05,399
Just like you,

92
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,319
I don't know where to go either.

93
00:08:19,639 --> 00:08:21,000
I need to return a call.

94
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:47,639
What's wrong?

95
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,639
What happened?

96
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:53,759
It's nothing.

97
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,320
My mom's sick.

98
00:09:00,799 --> 00:09:03,200
She needs money for treatment.

99
00:09:08,799 --> 00:09:10,399
That's why I can't leave.

100
00:09:13,919 --> 00:09:15,679
If it were just me,

101
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,559
it'd be a lot easier.

102
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:00,480
It's confirmed.

103
00:10:00,879 --> 00:10:03,080
The upfront cost is 100,000.

104
00:10:03,799 --> 00:10:04,840
Do you have any ideas?

105
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:27,879
I think he'll come to the office tonight.

106
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,240
Later, after work.

107
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,159
Where's Meng Hua?

108
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:32,840
I don't know.

109
00:10:32,919 --> 00:10:34,519
It seems he didn't return to the dorm last night, either.

110
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:36,919
I heard the manager say he quit.

111
00:10:38,279 --> 00:10:39,240
He quit?

112
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:40,639
Yeah.

113
00:10:43,759 --> 00:10:46,200
Is... is it because his mom is sick?

114
00:10:48,399 --> 00:10:49,200
I don't think so.

115
00:10:49,799 --> 00:10:52,360
Didn't his mom pass away a long time ago?

116
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:54,799
Yeah, that's what he said before.

117
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,120
What are you doing here?

118
00:11:45,559 --> 00:11:47,039
Why didn't you answer my calls?

119
00:11:55,799 --> 00:11:57,799
What are you going to do?

120
00:12:00,279 --> 00:12:00,919
I...

121
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:04,759
I just want you to answer one question.

122
00:12:06,639 --> 00:12:07,399
We...

123
00:12:08,919 --> 00:12:11,759
have so many colleagues at work.

124
00:12:13,559 --> 00:12:14,360
Why...

125
00:12:17,879 --> 00:12:19,799
why did it have to be me?

126
00:12:27,039 --> 00:12:29,440
Why did it have to be you?

127
00:12:31,679 --> 00:12:32,799
No reason.

128
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,200
I just thought you were easy to fool.

129
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,039
Where's the money?

130
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,120
I spent it all.

131
00:12:50,279 --> 00:12:51,039
Great.

132
00:12:52,919 --> 00:12:53,759
What do you mean?

133
00:12:54,919 --> 00:12:55,759
Fraud.

134
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,039
A huge amount.

135
00:12:58,039 --> 00:12:59,360
You can't pay it back.

136
00:13:00,559 --> 00:13:01,840
You're going to jail.

137
00:13:03,759 --> 00:13:05,399
This isn't fraud.

138
00:13:06,759 --> 00:13:10,320
At most, it's a credit dispute between us.

139
00:13:10,639 --> 00:13:11,399
If you don't mind the hassle,

140
00:13:11,399 --> 00:13:12,639
you can sue me in court.

141
00:13:14,279 --> 00:13:16,159
You used your mom's illness as an excuse

142
00:13:16,159 --> 00:13:17,120
to borrow money from me.

143
00:13:18,679 --> 00:13:20,440
But your mother was already dead.

144
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,039
Who can prove that?

145
00:13:25,519 --> 00:13:27,000
I remember when I asked you for the money,

146
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,159
I said it was to start a business.

147
00:13:35,519 --> 00:13:36,519
My mom is sick.

148
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:39,759
I need money for her medical bills.

149
00:13:41,279 --> 00:13:42,399
When did you record this?

150
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,039
I've been through a few things myself.

151
00:13:58,159 --> 00:13:59,759
I'm not as naive as you think.

152
00:14:01,519 --> 00:14:03,039
Then why did you still lend me money?

153
00:14:09,559 --> 00:14:10,320
Well, people...

154
00:14:13,039 --> 00:14:14,399
always tend to...

155
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,159
push their luck.

156
00:14:25,519 --> 00:14:28,360
About... about the money...

157
00:14:28,399 --> 00:14:30,159
Can... can you give me two more days?

158
00:14:30,159 --> 00:14:31,159
I... I'll find a way to pay you back.

159
00:14:31,159 --> 00:14:31,919
Don't bother.

160
00:14:33,799 --> 00:14:34,919
I've already called the police.

161
00:14:34,919 --> 00:14:36,320
You can talk to the cops.

162
00:14:36,679 --> 00:14:37,559
Didn't we...

163
00:15:02,039 --> 00:15:04,000
Why me?

164
00:15:06,519 --> 00:15:07,919
Need a reason?

165
00:15:09,679 --> 00:15:10,399
Mom.

166
00:15:11,159 --> 00:15:12,440
Why me?

167
00:15:13,399 --> 00:15:14,559
We were just unlucky.

168
00:15:14,559 --> 00:15:16,200
Just ran into some bad kids, that's all.

169
00:15:20,399 --> 00:15:22,399
Why did it have to be me?

170
00:15:23,159 --> 00:15:24,559
No reason.

171
00:15:26,799 --> 00:15:28,360
Just thought you were easy to fool.

172
00:15:45,639 --> 00:15:47,200
Meng Hua is a despicable scumbag,

173
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:50,399
but he did teach me one thing.

174
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,960
Some people do bad things

175
00:15:53,679 --> 00:15:55,399
simply because they're evil.

176
00:15:56,679 --> 00:15:57,840
They hurt others

177
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,639
for no reason at all.

178
00:16:00,879 --> 00:16:03,240
Zhou Minglei and Luo Qian's reappearance

179
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:05,120
also made me realize

180
00:16:06,159 --> 00:16:09,200
that running away won't solve the problem,

181
00:16:10,559 --> 00:16:13,639
because the problem won't let you go.

182
00:16:14,519 --> 00:16:18,080
So, I've decided to stop running.

183
00:16:18,399 --> 00:16:20,360
Hello. Rosemary Mashed Potatoes.

184
00:16:21,799 --> 00:16:22,399
Thank you.

185
00:16:28,919 --> 00:16:29,879
Is there anything else?

186
00:16:30,879 --> 00:16:31,559
Sorry to bother you.

187
00:16:31,919 --> 00:16:33,759
We're hosting an event here tomorrow.

188
00:16:34,039 --> 00:16:35,879
We invited a French pastry chef.

189
00:16:36,159 --> 00:16:37,559
Would you have time to attend?

190
00:16:40,519 --> 00:16:42,159
Sorry, the timing doesn't work for me.

191
00:16:43,519 --> 00:16:46,039
That's fine. You can leave an address.

192
00:16:46,399 --> 00:16:47,679
We'll refrigerate the pastries

193
00:16:47,679 --> 00:16:48,759
and express deliver them to your door.

194
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:02,480
"Keep the peace," "Return good for evil"...

195
00:17:03,039 --> 00:17:05,200
These survival lessons my mother taught me...

196
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:05,759
Thank you.

197
00:17:07,079 --> 00:17:07,480
Enjoy.

198
00:17:07,839 --> 00:17:09,640
...have only brought me endless humiliation.

199
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:13,480
This time, I'll make them reap what they sow.
